  "subject": {
    "id": "core-owned-population-fixture",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Move the population examples into a Core-owned fixture and state the profile rule in the seed.",
  "why": "Three pareto tests read handover/2026-09-03-core-population-v2/examples in place, so a handover directory pinned by OVR-000378 had become a Core fixture; docs/PRINCIPLES.md keeps fixtures inside Core and gives an archived spec no authority over tests. The eleven files are copied byte for byte to research/ontology_driven_kg_realization/fixtures/inspection_note_capture_v1 with a manifest and a README, the tests point there, and nothing under tests/ or src/ names the handover directory. The pinned examples themselves are untouched. validate_examples.py's check_profile had become a wrapper over DomainHistoryProfile.from_data, asserting the profile rule by running the implementation against itself; it now states the private-v1 rule and calls from_data afterwards only as a cross-check. The handover's profile section now states the shipped contract with its population.py line numbers instead of noting that P6 superseded the five-field shape."
}
